Maybe you can do something more concise like this, since `getOptionValue` its just accessing an object property
```js
ObjectDefineProperty(process.features, 'typescript', {
  __proto__: null,
  get() {
    if (!getOptionValue('--experimental-strip-types')) {
      return;
    }
    return getOptionValue('--experimental-transform-types') ? 'transform' : 'strip';
  },
  configurable: false,
  enumerable: true,
});
```
